      "content": "The \"performance\" is the lie he tells himself to keep breathing, the exhausting charade of being okay. If he stops playing, he stops pretending he deserves the effort. The darkness isn't a plot point; it's the only honest reflection of his fatigue. Let him drop the mask, not because he's defeated, but because the effort of wearing it has finally become unbearable.",
